{"id":"espagnol","lemma":"espagnol","pos":"adj","rank":2256,"glosses":["Spanish, from or otherwise related to Spain, its people etc."],"ipa":"/ɛs.pa.ɲɔl/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/64/Fr-espagnol.ogg/Fr-espagnol.ogg.mp3","forms":{"feminine":"espagnole","masculinePlural":"espagnols","femininePlural":"espagnoles"},"formAudio":{"espagnole":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/12/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-WikiLucas00-Espagnole.wav","espagnols":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Poslovitch-espagnols.wav","espagnoles":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dc/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Lyoko%C3%AF-espagnoles.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"L'espagnol est facile.","en":"Spanish is easy.","words":[{"g":"the / it"},null,{"g":"is","l":"être"},{"g":"easy, simple"}]},{"text":"J'aimerais avoir pu parler espagnol.","en":"I wish I could have spoken Spanish.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to love","l":"aimer"},{"g":"to have"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"pouvoir"},{"g":"to speak, talk"},null]},{"text":"Ils ont traversé la frontière espagnole.","en":"They crossed the border into Spain.","words":[{"g":"they"},{"g":"to have","l":"avoir"},{"g":"to cross, to go across","l":"traverser"},{"g":"the / her"},{"g":"boundary"},null]},{"text":"Elle me parla en espagnol.","en":"She spoke to me in Spanish.","words":[{"g":"she / it"},{"g":"me"},{"g":"to speak, talk","l":"parler"},{"g":"in / of it"},null]},{"text":"Il ne parle pas que français, mais aussi espagnol.","en":"He not only speaks French, but he speaks Spanish, too.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"not"},{"g":"to speak, talk","l":"parler"},null,null,{"g":"French"},{"g":"but"},{"g":"too, also, as well"},null],"phrases":[[3,5,"not that"]]}]}